    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-1",
      "note": "d_4>2g-2 and d_5=2g-2+n>2g-2 kill fibrewise H^1 of both graded pieces by Serre duality, hence R^1pi_*W=0; pi_*W is locally free of rank d_4+d_5+2-2g with arbitrary base change; Gamma is a disjoint union of n sections so pi_*(W|Gamma) is locally free of rank 2n; Fit_0(coker phi)=I_{2n}(phi). Verified.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-2",
      "note": "Independently reconstructed Sections 3-4. J subset I_e: e^*J=Fit_0(R^1pi_*omega tensor M_0^{-1})=Fit_0(M_0^{-1})=0, read as the extended ideal along the non-flat section. Reverse inclusion: for nonzero xi in H^1(O), the arc pullback Q_xi^{-1} is, on the underlying curve, an O_C-extension of O by O with class -xi (NOT an O_{C x D}-extension with class -xi*eps); after tensoring by omega the connecting map is cup with -xi over kappa, surjective by the perfect Serre pairing, so H^1(omega tensor Q_xi^{-1}) is 1-dimensional over kappa with eps acting by 0, giving i_xi^*J=(eps). Conormal spanning plus two Nakayama steps yield I_e subset J. The nonreduced scheme structure is genuine, not support-only, and matches the corroborated universal statement FND-0096.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-3",
      "note": "Tensoring with O_Gamma stays exact because W_5 is locally free; Gamma->B affine gives exact lower row; pi_*W->pi_*W_5 is surjective because R^1pi_*W_4=0 (deg W_4>2g-2); coker(phi_4)=R^1pi_*W_4(-Gamma)=0 because d_4-n>2g-2; snake lemma gives coker(phi)=coker(phi_5) with no global splitting, consistent with FND-0097/FND-0099 discipline.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-4",
      "note": "a_N^*(coker Phi)=R^1pi_*(omega tensor N^{-1}) tensor M^{-1} follows from Tor-independent derived base change (C_P->P flat); since R^1 is the top of an amplitude-[0,1] perfect complex, no Tor term lands in degree 1, so no fibre-h^1 constancy is needed. Fitting ideals commute with arbitrary base change and are invariant under invertible twist; x_1-rigidification gives the T-point criterion N_T=pi_T^*M_T; smooth-atlas descent of quasi-coherent ideals is standard. No coarse-space assertion is made.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-5",
      "note": "Fibres O(4)+O(5) give F(-5) fibres O(-1)+O, so s_*F(-5) is invertible with R^1=0 and base-change-compatible formation; the counit s^*s_*F(-5)->F(-5) is fibrewise the inclusion into the O summand, constant rank one, hence a subbundle with locally free quotient. Dualizing, pulling back, and twisting gives the filtered W; the residual pi^*-base twist does not change fibre degrees, so SRC-0004's deg(W_f)=4g+12-4f yields d_4=20, d_5=16 at g=6.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-6",
      "note": "Tensoring the hypothesized CE resolution by script-W and using det(F) tensor F^vee canonically = F (rank two) gives 0->O_X(-2) tensor p^*F->p^*End(F)->I_C tensor script-W->0. H^i(P^2,O(-2))=0 for i=0,1,2, so Rp_*O_X(-2)=0 in every degree and Rp_*(I_C tensor script-W)=End(F)[0]. Applying Rp_* to 0->I_C tensor script-W->script-W->i_*W->0 (with Rp_*script-W concentrated in degree 0 since H^{>0}(P^2,O(2))=0) gives 0->End(F)->p_*script-W->gamma_*W->0, and s_* then displays R^1s_*End(F) as the exact obstruction. Rank check: on a balanced fibre h^0(End(F))=4, so q_*script-W has rank 26+4=30, consistent.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-7",
      "note": "With R^1s_*End(F)=0, (8.4) gives surjectivity of r; im(phi composed with r)=im(phi), hence canonical cokernel equality. Base-change compatibility: q_*script-W commutes by explicit hypothesis, pi_*W by Section 2, CE constructions fibrewise constant, and a pullback of the surjection r remains surjective by right-exactness, so the Fitting equality persists after arbitrary locally Noetherian base change.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-8",
      "note": "End(O(4)+O(5))=O^2+O(1)+O(-1) has H^1=0 on every geometric fibre. Top-degree base change identifies geometric fibres of R^1s_*End(F) with fibrewise H^1 (R^1 is the top of a perfect amplitude-[0,1] complex), and Nakayama kills the sheaf; the same holds after arbitrary base change. No global splitting of F is used, discharging the FND-0097 concern.",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "CLM-0065-9",
      "note": "Combination of the confirmed claims: at (6,6), 20-6=14>10 and 16-6=10=2g-2, ranks 26->12, obstruction vanishes automatically, and Fit_0(coker phi)=a_N^*I_e identifies the balanced ambient failure scheme scheme-theoretically with the relative incidence O_C(Gamma)=W_5 tensor omega^{-1} (relative isomorphism = triviality of N in Pic^0, i.e. up to pullback from the base).",
      "verdict": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
