      "statement": "For a degree-four CE embedding whose ideal has the standard resolution 0->O_X(-4) tensor p^*det(F)->O_X(-2) tensor p^*F->I_C->0, tensoring by script-W=O_X(2) tensor p^*F^vee and pushing along the P2-bundle gives canonically 0->End(F)->p_*script-W->gamma_*W->0, because Rp_*O_X(-2)=0 in every degree and det(F) tensor F^vee=F for rank two. Hence the exact obstruction to surjectivity of q_*script-W->pi_*W is R^1s_*End(F); the equation-bundle base-change hypothesis alone does not imply surjectivity, and fibrewise balanced F=O(4)+O(5) forces the obstruction to vanish without any global splitting. Downstream ambient comparisons should cite the obstruction in this form.",
      "status": "candidate",
      "summary": "For a degree-four CE embedding whose ideal has the standard resolution 0->O_X(-4) tensor p^*det(F)->O_X(-2) tensor p^*F->I_C->0, tensoring by script-W=O_X(2) tensor p^*F^vee and pushing along the P2-bundle gives canonically 0->End(F)->p_*script-W->gamma_*W->0, because Rp_*O_X(-2)=0 in every degree and det(F) tensor F^vee=F for rank two. Hence the exact obstruction to surjectivity of q_*script-W->pi_*W is R^1s_*End(F); the equation-bundle base-change hypothesis alone does not imply surjectivity, and fibrewise balanced F=O(4)+O(5) forces the obstruction to vanish without any global splitting. Downstream ambient comparisons should cite the obstruction in this form.",
